From 7b20a40cc3ffb29e21d301368ffbd8b4fd3ff6c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 02:36:24 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 63/73] menu_scroll: Scrolls menus that extend beyond the
 screen, like Window Maker.

When a menu, with its open submenus, extends beyond the usable area and the
pointer is at the edge of the output, next to the menu: The menu's window
slides in steps of 8 pixels every 10 ms, until its far end is within the
usable area. Like Window Maker does when the pointer reaches the screen's
edge. This applies to the root menu and to context menus, eg. one with a
submenu taller than the screen.

Adds wlmtk_menu_get_extents, the box covered by a menu and its open
submenus, and wlmtk_util_box_union.
